	(text "NOTE: CELL_BATPRESZ/CELL_CONF CONFIGURATION\n---------------------------------\nCurrent Config: 4S (16.8V)\nR_high (to REGN): 100k (1%)\nR_low  (to GND) : 300k (1%)\n\nRatio = 300k / (100k + 300k) = 0.75 (75%)\n\nDATASHEET REFERENCE (Table 9-1)\n---------------------------------------------\n| Cell | Pin Voltage | Charge V | SYSOVP    |\n| Count| (% of VDDA) | Limit    | Threshold |\n|------|-------------|----------|-----------|\n|  4S  |     75%     | 16.800 V |  19.5 V   |\n|  3S  |     55%     | 12.592 V |  19.5 V   |\n|  2S  |     40%     |  8.400 V |  12.0 V   |\n|  1S  |     25%     |  4.192 V |   5.0 V   |\n---------------------------------------------\n*WARNING: Use 1% resistors. Incorrect detection\n leads to wrong SYSOVP and charging lockout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -68.58 141.732 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8118c771-fb20-4144-bbb0-5be3e9706936")
	)
	(text "USB C PD CONTROLLER CONFIG\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.196 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "86638c2b-0209-4da8-99c4-77ee5495ffe1")
	)
	(text "/* ==========================================================================\n   BQ25713 PINOUT REFERENCE & FUNCTIONAL GROUPS\n   ========================================================================== */\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   1. POWER PATH & SWITCHING (High Current / High Voltage)\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// VBUS (Pin 1)\n// Main Input Power (from USB-C Connector). Range: 3.5V - 24V.\n\n// VSYS (Pin 22)\n// System Output Power. Connects to the system load (3.3V regulators, etc.).\n// REGULATED output (maintained even if battery is removed, provided VBUS exists).\n\n// SW1 (Pin 32)\n// Switching Node 1 (Input/Buck Side). Connects to Inductor.\n\n// SW2 (Pin 23)\n// Switching Node 2 (Battery/Boost Side). Connects to Inductor.\n\n// PGND (Pin 27)\n// Power Ground. High-current return path for MOSFETs. \n// MUST connect to Thermal Pad (EP) via star-ground.\n\n// EP (Pin 33 / Thermal Pad)\n// Exposed Pad. Main Thermal dissipation and common Ground reference.\n\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   2. MOSFET GATE DRIVERS (The \"Nerves\")\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// HIDRV1 (Pin 31) / LODRV1 (Pin 29)\n// Gate Drivers for Q1 (High-Side) and Q2 (Low-Side). \n// Controls the \"Buck\" leg (Input side).\n\n// HIDRV2 (Pin 24) / LODRV2 (Pin 26)\n// Gate Drivers for Q3 (High-Side) and Q4 (Low-Side).\n// Controls the \"Boost\" leg (Battery side).\n\n// BTST1 (Pin 30) / BTST2 (Pin 25)\n// Bootstrap Capacitors. Provides floating supply to drive High-Side MOSFETs.\n// Connect 47nF capacitor from BTSTx to SWx.\n\n// BATDRV (Pin 21)\n// Battery Isolation FET Driver. Drives the P-Ch or N-Ch FET between VSYS and BATT.\n// Used for Power Path Management (disconnects battery if VBUS is present but weak).\n\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   3. CURRENT SENSING (Differential Pairs - Route Carefully!)\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// ACP (Pin 3) / ACN (Pin 2)\n// Input Current Sense. Connect across input shunt resistor (R_SNS_IN).\n// Measures current coming from the USB adapter.\n\n// SRP (Pin 20) / SRN (Pin 19)\n// Battery Current Sense. Connect across battery shunt resistor (R_SNS_BAT).\n// Measures Charge (current into batt) and Discharge (current out of batt).\n\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   4. LOGIC & CONTROL (Connect to MCU / TPS25750)\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// SDA (Pin 12) / SCL (Pin 13)\n// I2C Communication Interface.\n// Connect to TPS25750 (Master) or STM32 (if manual control needed).\n\n// EN_OTG (Pin 5) - Digital Input\n// Direction Control.\n// LOW (0V)  = Charge Mode (Sink power from USB to Battery).\n// HIGH (3V3)= OTG Mode (Source power from Battery to USB).\n\n// CHRG_OK (Pin 4) - Open-Drain Output\n// Active HIGH (requires Pull-Up).\n// Signals that a valid Input Source (VBUS) is present and qualified.\n// Use as Wake-Up interrupt for MCU.\n\n// PROCHOT (Pin 11) - Open-Drain Output\n// Active LOW (requires Pull-Up).\n// \"Processor Hot\" / Emergency Throttle.\n// Goes LOW if: System Overload, Battery Critical, or Thermal Shutdown.\n\n// CELL_BATPRESZ (Pin 18) - Analog/Digital Multifunction\n// 1. At Startup: Checks resistor to GND to configure Cell Count (2S, 3S, 4S).\n// 2. Runtime: Detects Battery removal.\n\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   5. TELEMETRY ANALOG OUTPUTS (Connect to MCU ADC)\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// PSYS (Pin 10)\n// Power Monitor. Output voltage proportional to Total System Power.\n// V_PSYS = K_PSYS * (V_SYS * I_SYS).\n\n// IBAT (Pin 9)\n// Battery Current Monitor. Output voltage proportional to Battery Current.\n// Positive for Charging, Negative (or offset) for Discharging.\n\n// IADPT (Pin 8)\n// Input Current Monitor. Output voltage proportional to VBUS Current.\n\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   6. BIASING & COMPENSATION (Internal Housekeeping)\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n// REGN (Pin 28)\n// Internal LDO Output (6V). Powers the Gate Drivers.\n// REQUIRES 4.7uF ceramic capacitor to GND close to pin.\n\n// VDDA (Pin 7)\n// Analog Supply. Requires clean filtering (RC filter recommended).\n\n// ILIM_HIZ (Pin 6) - Analog Input\n// Sets Hardware Input Current Limit via resistor divider.\n// Pulling HIGH (> 2.2V) puts converter in Hi-Z (High Impedance/Sleep) mode.\n\n// COMP1 (Pin 16) / COMP2 (Pin 17)\n// Loop Compensation. Connect RC network to GND to stabilize voltage/current loops.\n// See Datasheet for calculation (typically ~10k Ohm + ~4.7nF)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.526 -121.412 0)
